A misspelt `core.autonomy` in the vault's config.yaml stops the playbook render in band: the STOP
notice alone on stdout, exit 0, and the fixture playbook's preamble never appears.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/home/Claude/probe/config.yaml --
core:
  autonomy: autonomus
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-autonomy/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-autonomy
title: Autonomy
summary: Must not render with an unknown autonomy mode.
---

Preamble that a working gate suppresses.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-autonomy/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  only: []
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-autonomy/only/prompt.md --
---
name: only
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-autonomy
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
**STOP — tell the user:** `core.autonomy` is `autonomus`; it must be `supervised` or `autonomous`. Fix it in the config tier that sets it, then retry.
-- stderr --
